disk_generic: let a backend say its medium can be taken out

A disk_generic is answered for by three Sys_ routines that never ask it:
SysIsFixedDisk() and SysIsDiskInserted() return true outright and
SysEject() ignores it, so every backend is a fixed disk with its medium
welded in. That was true of the ones that existed — sparse bundles and
VHDs are files — but it is not a property of the interface, and it is why
a backend cannot be a CD-ROM drive or a floppy drive.

Three virtuals with the old answers as their defaults, so nothing existing
changes, and the four call sites that were answering on the backend's
behalf now ask it. SysGetFileSize() goes the same way: it was returning a
size cached at open time, which is wrong for anything whose medium can be
swapped for a different one.

mihaip/macemu carries this (branch infinite-mac-kanjitalk755), where the
backend is the browser and the user really does swap disks.

diff --git a/BasiliskII/src/Unix/disk_unix.h b/BasiliskII/src/Unix/disk_unix.h
index 6c427881..838cc1d4 100644
--- a/BasiliskII/src/Unix/disk_unix.h
+++ b/BasiliskII/src/Unix/disk_unix.h
@@ -37,6 +37,15 @@ struct disk_generic {
 	virtual size_t read(void *buf, loff_t offset, size_t length) = 0;
 	virtual size_t write(void *buf, loff_t offset, size_t length) = 0;
 	virtual loff_t size() = 0;
+
+	// A generic disk is a fixed one with its medium in it unless it says
+	// otherwise. Every existing backend is exactly that, so the defaults keep
+	// them working unchanged; a backend that is a CD-ROM drive, a floppy drive
+	// or anything the user can swap overrides them, and the Mac then gets a
+	// truthful answer through SysIsFixedDisk() and SysIsDiskInserted().
+	virtual bool is_media_present() { return true; }
+	virtual bool is_fixed_disk() { return true; }
+	virtual void eject() { }
 };
 
